    "page": 9,
    "quote": "he offeror must draw up an offer document containing adequate information in order for the shareholders of\nthe Company to be able to form a well-founded opinion on the offer.\nThe offer must as a general rule, provide equal treatment to shareholders of the same share class. The offer\ndocument shall at least address a number of identified issues, such as (but not limited to):\na. The identity of the offeror(s),\nb. The offeror(s)’ current holding of shares in the Company or control over voting rights,\nc. The price offered (cash or shares),\nd. Financing,\ne. Future plans for the Company, including possible restructurings and employment perspectives, and\nf. Details of related party arrangements regarding use of the voting rights of the Company.\nThe acceptance period in the offer must be at least four weeks and may not exceed ten weeks. The offer period\nmay, however, be extended beyond ten weeks, provided that the terms of the offer are changed or if\ncompeting offers are submitted.\nAn offeror’",
